        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63328381?u=94bf21f5823e17bc14d7e82e61e77b0698ad6686&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Update the <code class=\"notranslate\">Signature</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">Accept-Signature</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">Signature-Input</code> headers to point to the RFC9421 rather than a WICG draft. Also <code class=\"notranslate\">Signed-Headers</code> seems to to not be used, so changing in favor of <code class=\"notranslate\">Signature-Input</code> which is defined. Based on <a href=\"https://github.com/WICG/webpackage/issues/713#issue-1142375682\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/WICG/webpackage/issues/713/hovercard\">this issue</a>, the WICG http message signatures seems somewhat obsoleted?</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Points to the adopted RFC rather than draft documents</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">n/a</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">(<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1142375682\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/WICG/webpackage/issues/713\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/WICG/webpackage/issues/713/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/WICG/webpackage/issues/713\">WICG/webpackage#713</a>)<br>\n(<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2796270897\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37701\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/37701/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37701\">#37701</a>)</p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41530",
            "title": "update signature headers to point to rfc9421",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-14T14:06:57.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-14T14:06:32.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "aamuley",
                "url": "https://github.com/aamuley"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF145 supports Trusted Types in early beta in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1992941\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1992941</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note, experimental feature, and updates the API overview page.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is a minimal update to provide a coherent story, with links to most affected interfaces. There are still quite a few interfaces that actually need updates but they will come in follow on PRs.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3510273732\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41507/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41507\">#41507</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41518",
            "title": "FF145 Relnote: Trusted Types early beta",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-31T18:06:01.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-14T02:09:17.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In our <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FedCM_API/IDP_integration\" rel=\"nofollow\">Identity provider integration with FedCM</a> page, we mention the <code class=\"notranslate\">approved_clients</code> field of the accounts list endpoint JSON, but we don't say what it does.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR aims to add that detail.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #38259.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2867261553\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/38259\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/38259/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/38259\">#38259</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41496",
            "title": "Add use case details for approved_clients field",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-13T13:34:52.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-13T13:33:18.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3054066?u=00a2aabab440d4b81da911b9b7bec6012d9284c0&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updated examples to use <code class=\"notranslate\">document.importNode()</code> exclusively, and references to refer to both <code class=\"notranslate\">importNode</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">Node.cloneNode</code>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">document.importNode</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">Node.cloneNode</code> are largely similar, but have one important difference; the timing of when the node is <em>adopted</em>. When using <code class=\"notranslate\">Node.cloneNode()</code>, the content isn't adopted until it's either explicitly adopted or when it's appended to the document, so at a later point after calling <code class=\"notranslate\">cloneNode()</code>. This falls into an edge-case annoyance where calling <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CustomElementRegistry/upgrade\" rel=\"nofollow\">upgrade</a> on nodes that aren't yet adopted causes them to not actually get upgraded. This real example from the Web Components discord demonstrates the edge-case:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"class MyEl extends HTMLElement {\n  constructor() {super(); console.log('MyEl constructor')}\n}\ncustomElements.define('my-el', MyEl)\n\nconst template = document.createElement('template')\ntemplate.innerHTML = '&lt;my-el&gt;&lt;/my-el&gt;'\n\nconst frag = template.content.cloneNode(true)\n\nconsole.log(customElements.get('my-el')) // MyEl\n\ncustomElements.upgrade(frag) // crickets\nconsole.log('My el constructor should have ran already')\n\ndocument.body.append(frag) // logs &quot;MyEl constructor&quot;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">class</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">MyEl</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">extends</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">HTMLElement</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">constructor</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span><span class=\"pl-smi\">super</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">console</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">log</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">'MyEl constructor'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">customElements</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">define</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">'my-el'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">MyEl</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">template</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">document</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">createElement</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">'template'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">template</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">innerHTML</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">'&lt;my-el&gt;&lt;/my-el&gt;'</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">frag</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">template</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">content</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">cloneNode</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">console</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">log</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">customElements</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">get</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">'my-el'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-c\">// MyEl</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">customElements</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">upgrade</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">frag</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-c\">// crickets</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">console</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">log</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">'My el constructor should have ran already'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">document</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">body</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">append</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">frag</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-c\">// logs \"MyEl constructor\"</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you change from <code class=\"notranslate\">content.cloneNode()</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">document.importNode()</code> then the constructor will run and the content is upgraded correctly.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So we would like to update the examples to show <code class=\"notranslate\">document.importNode()</code> being used by default, and also update references/links to show it as an option next to cloneNode.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Web components discord discussion <a href=\"https://discord.com/channels/767813449048260658/767813449048260661/1421037073829199994\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://discord.com/channels/767813449048260658/767813449048260661/1421037073829199994</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41441",
            "title": "Change cloneNode references to importNode",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-21T23:40:12.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-08T18:55:18.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "frehner",
                "url": "https://github.com/frehner"
            }
        }
    ]
}